From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] socket: listen on hostfwd with SOMAXCONN, not 1

What: listen on a hostfwd socket with a backlog of SOMAXCONN instead
of 1.

Why: with a backlog of 1, macOS resets one of two connections that
reach the forwarded port at once, before libslirp accepts it. The guest
never sees the lost connection. Two ssh connections at once to a VM on
the user network lost one with "Connection reset by peer" in about 3
rounds of 4. A single connection never failed. With SOMAXCONN,
`netstat -Lan -p tcp` shows the queue as 0/0/128 instead of 0/0/1, and
the forward loses no connections.

Upstream: not merged upstream yet. libslirp master has
SlirpConfig.hostfwd_listen_backlog in unreleased config version 7, but
its default is still 1, and QEMU 11.1 passes version 6. This patch
applies to libslirp 4.9.4 after the other four libslirp patches and
does not depend on them.

Test: app/runtime/Tests/net/test-slirp-hostfwd-burst.sh. The runtime
build runs it on a real QEMU with -netdev user and no guest. It opens 2
connections at once to a host forward for 30 rounds.

diff --git a/src/socket.c b/src/socket.c
index 1451116..afb71aa 100644
--- a/src/socket.c
+++ b/src/socket.c
@@ -930,7 +930,9 @@ struct socket *tcpx_listen(Slirp *slirp,
         (haddr->sa_family == AF_INET6 && slirp_socket_set_v6only(s, (flags & SS_HOSTFWD_V6ONLY) != 0) < 0) ||
         (slirp_socket_set_fast_reuse(s) < 0) ||
         (bind(s, haddr, haddrlen) < 0) ||
-        (listen(s, 1) < 0)) {
+        /* With a backlog of 1, macOS resets one of two connections that
+         * arrive at the same moment, before slirp accepts it. */
+        (listen(s, SOMAXCONN) < 0)) {
         int tmperrno = errno; /* Don't clobber the real reason we failed */
         if (have_valid_socket(s)) {
             closesocket(s);
